codex
The paper’s precise easy cases are now clear: full feasibility MILP is only practical on very small instances; 3×3–6×6 were solved, 7×7–8×8 were not completed in the reported runs; border optimization is effectively one-dimensional; and a fixed nonadjacent-position neighborhood becomes bipartite matching. The proposed 14×14 full placement-and-rotation regime avoids those cases, and its palette grows with board size, so it is not a fixed-small-parameter regime. I’m now stress-testing the planted distribution with stronger propagation than the draft originally used.
