codex
The audit found and fixed two substantive issues before rerunning gates: the random-restart attack now builds edge-consistent partial boards instead of sampling almost-certainly-invalid complete noise, and the canonical key now handles the square board’s reflection symmetry with a carried witness test. The rendered gray-border rule is also stated exactly as the verifier enforces it. I’m running the full 200,000-sample and 40-million-node gate suite now.
