Key results:

- Inverse-generated native edge-matching puzzles based on the paper’s feasibility formulation. [Full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1709.00252v2)
- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: 0/8 each.
- CSP/DPLL baseline: 40,000,000 nodes, 38.66 seconds, no solution.
- Answer: 196 elements, 758 characters.
- Canonicalization passed 60 reflection/relabeling witness checks.
- Hardness basis references the cited unsigned edge-matching NP-completeness theorem. [Demaine–Demaine paper](https://people.csail.mit.edu/edemaine/papers/Jigsaw_GC/paper.pdf)

The only blocker is Step 4: all 12 harness calls across bare, hinted, and placebo arms returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” These error-only transcripts are preserved but are not valid hardness evidence. After restoring quota, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/1709.00252
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1709_00252.py
```

No `REJECTED.md` was created because the family itself passed; the blockage is external.
